   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let m(x) = (x^2 - 3) v(x), where v(x) = x/(2x + 1), for x not equal to -1/2. What is the value of m'(1)?"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         4,
         9
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Take u = x^2 - 3, so u' = 2x. The quotient rule gives v'(x) = ((2x + 1)(1) - x(2))/(2x + 1)^2 = 1/(2x + 1)^2.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            1,
            [
               "Power",
               [
                  "Add",
                  [
                     "Multiply",
                     2,
                     "x"
                  ],
                  1
               ],
               2
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "At x = 1: u = -2, u' = 2, v = 1/3 and v' = 1/9.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            9
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The product rule gives m'(1) = u' v + u v' = 2(1/3) + (-2)(1/9).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Rational",
               -2,
               9
            ],
            [
               "Rational",
               2,
               3
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "Over the common denominator 9 this is 6/9 - 2/9 = 4/9.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            4,
            9
         ]
      }
